From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:57:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 69/86] Optional images from the web in the Markdown preview

New setting "Load images from the web in Markdown previews" (Settings,
Markdown; config key markdown_remote_images, off by default). With it
off nothing is fetched and remote images stay alt text chips. With it
on, https images (no other scheme) are fetched through GIO's gvfs HTTP
backend, already in the tree via cosmic-files (gio becomes an optional
dependency of the gvfs feature): on a background thread, cancelled
after 15 s, at most 10 MB, PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP/BMP/ICO/SVG only. Results
stay in memory for the session; the preview checks back every 250 ms
while fetches are pending. A failure keeps the chip and logs one
warning per image naming the host and the reason.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

